raw_text = "~ start
Player: This poster says I can help families in crisis by scanning the QR code. What should I do?

- Scan it and carefully check the URL preview before opening
	Player: My phone will show me the link first, so I can check it there.
	System: Safer, but not the best choice. Shortened URLs can hide important details, and 92% of users in one study still continued with shortened phishing URLs.
	=> END

- Look over the poster for anything suspicious before scanning
	Player: The poster looks professional, and nothing seems obviously wrong.
	System: Not enough! The poster itself can be the \"pretext\" that makes the QR code seem trustworthy.
	=> END

- Verify the fundraiser through an official workplace source first
	Player: I'll check with the company or organizer before interacting with the QR code.
	System: Best choice! You verified the source instead of trusting the poster or hidden link.
	=> END"
metadata/dialogue_manager_version = "3.10.4"
